& [Delineation]
  + parsing determines whether input has the closed wire shape
  + validation determines whether supplied forms and their lineage replay coherently
  + observation records a claimed effect but does not prove it independently
  + verification disposition records the result of separately supplied checks
  + CLI exit status describes request processing, never artifact authorization or safety

& [CriticalReroute]
  + a validator that silently derives missing authorization, observation, or receipt forms would become an ungoverned author
  + Slice7 therefore accepts complete forms and only replays existing pure validators
  + build execution and receipt construction remain separate caller responsibilities

& [DataDrivenDesign]
  + [keys] protocol_version request_id operation stage artifact_id verification_receipt_id
  + [roots] seed IR candidate plan native projection build plan capability sandbox approval authorization observation ledger artifact receipt verifier plan observation and receipt digests
  + [relations] request owns bundle bundle replays lineage lineage reaches stage stage reported_by response
  + [states] input_refused lifecycle_refused artifact_valid verification_valid
  + [constraints] one request one operation complete stage closure exact identities bounded bytes closed enums deny_unknown_fields deterministic ordering

& [DualHemisphereReview]
  + [expansive] later protocols may validate attention procedures inference-host projections signatures admission receipts FPGA artifacts or remote build attestations
  + [expansive] adapters may later expose the same request through MCP HTTP or llama.cpp tool calls
  + [convergent] P0 supports one native artifact lifecycle, two explicit operations, JSON stdin or one file, and pure replay only
  + [convergent] no general workflow interpreter, auto-discovery, partial repair, effect runner, or remote adapter enters this slice

& [SevenFoldExplosion]
  + [fold_1_identity] bind request operation protocol and every lifecycle identity without aliases
  + [fold_2_shape] close JSON schemas, stage completeness, option correspondence, byte limits, and trailing data
  + [fold_3_replay] execute validators only in causal dependency order and stop at the earliest fault
  + [fold_4_honesty] separate coherent representation from observed truth, verification passage, safety, and authority
  + [fold_5_security] accept public trust material only and preserve all non-authority and local-ledger limitations
  + [fold_6_interface] keep machine stdout deterministic, stderr diagnostic, and exits semantically distinct
  + [fold_7_growth] retain a stable seam for later MCP or inference-host adapters without coupling them now

& [ConstraintLedger]
  + reuse Slice5 and Slice6 forms and validators rather than duplicate their laws
  + never deserialize private signing keys or ambient runner configuration
  + validation mode requires artifact closure; verification mode requires the entire verification closure
  + failed or unresolved verification can still be a valid receipt and must remain distinguishable from a passing receipt
  + fixed response non-authority must deny execution signing admission installation deployment safety truth and global atomic consumption

& [PruningTrace]
  + pruned automatic repair, default synthesis, partial lifecycle validation, dynamic plugin loading, model calls, filesystem scans, process execution, remote calls, and artifact launch
  + pruned a shared operation with ambiguous optional fields in favor of explicit artifact and verification operations
  + pruned production naming in favor of compiler-lab until host effects and stable protocol compatibility are separately governed

& [Uncertainty]
  + JSON bundle size may be large because exact replay currently carries full upstream forms
  + later content-addressed custody handles can compress transport only after a trusted registry boundary is selected
  + global single-use authorization enforcement still requires an external transactional authority

& [Exhaustion]
  + [gain_delta] one callable authority-preserving machine seam over the existing native lifecycle
  + [exhaustion_state] phase_locked_for_read_only_native_lifecycle_protocol
  + [growth_seed] expose the proven protocol through a separately governed tool adapter or content-addressed custody layer
